From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shikosu <teovidal01@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 17:09:36 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] aot: an svc no longer leaks into the next dc/ic, per-thread
 memory counters, last-region cache; jump tables bounded by a ccmp guard

hyper_call was never cleared after an svc, so the next SYS (dc civac) re-ran the svc handler (phantom ArbitrateLock). The read/write counters were one shared atomic hit by every guest load and store of every thread (Xenoblade 2: a frame a second); they are per-thread slots now, and guest() tries the region the thread hit last. A compound guard (cmp w4,#0 ; ccmp w8,#3) bounds a switch by its larger immediate (PadManager::makePadData). Found booting Xenoblade Chronicles 2.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Upstream-Status: pending
Reason: S7bis: silent audio, time, first frames presented by Xenoblade Chronicles 2, and AOT runtime fixes found doing it; tests use synthetic code and fake guest memory, no game data
Issue: none yet (NX2Linux, branch swann/jalon-s7bis-xc2)

